#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:1
msgid "How to Update Unicode Tables"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:3
msgid ""
"LLVM and Clang use a subset of the [Unicode Character Database](https://"
"www.unicode.org/ucd/) (UCD) for identifiers, `\\N{...}` named characters, "
"diagnostic column width, and simple case folding. The corresponding tables "
"are generated from the UCD into Clang and LLVM Support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:8
msgid "Downloading the Unicode data"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:10
msgid "Download the following files:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:19
msgid "Unzip `ucd.nounihan.flat.zip` to get `ucd.nounihan.flat.xml`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:21
msgid "Building the generators"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:23
msgid ""
"Build the generators from an LLVM build directory that has utilities enabled "
"(`LLVM_BUILD_UTILS`, the default) and libxml2 (`LLVM_ENABLE_LIBXML2`, also "
"the default):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:31
msgid "Then run them from the `llvm-project` root as shown below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:33
msgid "Character properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:35
msgid ""
"`UnicodeCharSetsGenerator` writes the identifier character sets used by the "
"lexer (`XID_Start`, `XID_Continue`, and the mathematical compatibility "
"notation profile) and the printable / formatting / combining / East-Asian-"
"width sets used by LLVM Support."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:48
msgid ""
"The C99 and C11 identifier tables and the whitespace table in `clang/lib/Lex/"
"UnicodeCharSets.h` are maintained by hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:51
msgid "Character names"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:53
msgid ""
"`UnicodeNameMappingGenerator` writes the name-to-codepoint trie used by "
"`\\N{...}` and `llvm::sys::unicode::nameToCodepointStrict` / "
"`nameToCodepointLooseMatching`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:63
msgid ""
"Algorithmically derived names (`CJK UNIFIED IDEOGRAPH-*`, and so on) are not "
"in those files. Update `GeneratedNamesDataTable` in `llvm/lib/Support/"
"UnicodeNameToCodepoint.cpp` from `DerivedName.txt`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:67
msgid "Case folding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:69
msgid ""
"`llvm/utils/unicode-case-fold.py` fetches `CaseFolding.txt` and writes `llvm/"
"lib/Support/UnicodeCaseFold.cpp`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../HowToUpdateUnicodeTables.md:78
msgid ""
"After regenerating the tables, update `llvm/unittests/Support/"
"UnicodeTest.cpp` and `clang/test/Lexer/unicode.c` for new characters and "
"changed name ranges."
msgstr ""
